th sides", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[39, 308], [532, 310], [532, 329], [39, 327]]}, {"text": "endlessly,as there are infinite positive and negative real numbers. As in the set of real", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[39, 327], [536, 328], [536, 347], [39, 346]]}, {"text": "numbers, we have positive, negative and zero, so we must choose a point to represent the", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[39, 346], [562, 348], [562, 367], [39, 365]]}, {"text": "number zero on it. For a real number line, this point zero acts as an origin.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[39, 364], [465, 367], [465, 387], [39, 383]]}, {"text": "'Mark the positive numbers to the right side and the negative numbers to the left of 0.", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[38, 452], [537, 459], [536, 478], [38, 471]]}, {"text": "Negative Direction", "conf": 0.849, "box": [[127, 492], [229, 494], [228, 510], [126, 508]]}, {"text": "Positive Direction", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[380, 496], [477, 498], [477, 515], [380, 513]]}, {"text": "+1", "conf": 0.587, "box": [[329, 538], [346, 538], [346, 556], [329, 556]]}, {"text": "+2", "conf": 0.664, "box": [[367, 540], [386, 540], [386, 556], [367, 556]]}, {"text": "E+", "conf": 0.527, "box": [[404, 542], [426, 542], [426, 558], [404, 558]]}, {"text": "+4", "conf": 0.504, "box": [[435, 543], [461, 543], [461, 558], [435, 558]]}, {"text": "+5", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[476, 543], [496, 543], [496, 556], [476, 556]]}, {"text": "Negiative Integers", "conf": 0.839, "box": [[128, 565], [225, 569], [224, 586], [128, 582]]}, {"text": "Positive Integers", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[383, 570], [473, 573], [473, 590], [382, 587]]}, {"text": "Origin", "conf": 0.74, "box": [[283, 600], [322, 602], [321, 619], [282, 617]]}, {"text": "Next mark points on both sides of the origin with equal distances between them.", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[42, 623], [509, 634], [509, 654], [42, 642]]}, {"text": "-6-5", "conf": 0.612, "box": [[78, 681], [146, 681], [146, 699], [78, 699]]}, {"text": "+4", "conf": 0.639, "box": [[442, 6